{
  "name": "cloud_volume_sweep",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "§25c against §25b at close zoom across the afternoon, both arms at every hour (issue #144). BUILT BECAUSE cloud_volume_perf's BLOWOUT LOOKED LIKE AN ACCUMULATION AND IS EQUALLY CONSISTENT WITH A SUN THAT MOVED. That scenario never re-issues SetTime and its seven 300-frame Profile windows each advance it, so its four volumetric arms were shot at four different unrecorded hours -- mean brightness rising 107/121/137/164 while the baked arms beside them rose only 111/109/115/122. Here the hour is STATED rather than inherited, sun_elevation is pinned beside every frame so a later clock change fails loudly instead of silently re-shooting the sweep somewhere else, and both renderers are captured at each hour so the DIVERGENCE is the measurement rather than either frame alone. No Profile steps.",
